cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "lstm-forecast: A leakage-free LSTM stock forecaster and an honest report of the NULL result"
abstract: >-
  A pure, typed Python rebuild of the classic LSTM stock-price-prediction
  project, done without leakage. It forecasts the next-day log-return (never the
  price level), validates with a purged, embargoed, per-fold-scaled walk-forward,
  and tests honestly against a random-walk / persistence baseline. The documented,
  literature-backed result is the NULL: a properly validated LSTM (and
  LSTM+Attention) does not beat persistence out-of-sample on return-space error
  (MASE >= 1) or directional accuracy (Diebold-Mariano insignificant). No
  price-level R-squared is reported. The shipped model is trained on synthetic
  random-walk data and served via ONNX / onnxruntime (TensorFlow is train-only).
